Feature: F8 target — the TEKO_TARGET boundary (compile-fail; R2 honest error, teko-target-crosslink-0.3.1.md §0)

  # An unrecognised TEKO_TARGET must be a COMPILE error naming the value AND listing the supported
  # set — never a silent mis-lower to some other object format (the pre-0.3.1 arm64/Mach-O fallback,
  # which is how a linux x86_64 host came to emit a Mach-O arm64 object).
  Scenario: an unsupported TEKO_TARGET is an honest compile error listing the supported set
    Given backend = "own"
    Given target = "bogus-arch"
    Given source inline = """
    exit(42)
    """
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "unsupported TEKO_TARGET"

